-- title:
--   Checking terminal witnesses from a stored reporting frontier
-- statement:
--   Write $S,\Omega,\Delta$ for machine space, word magnitude, and depth limits. Let $I$ be a finite set of raw items, $w$ a wanted label, and $k\le J$. Suppose the retained frontier at level $k$ has its exact count, query mask, and left/right prefix-mask arrays stored at root $a$, with the correct capacity in $a+3$. Independently, let stored integer arrays $L,R$, integer $a_0,\delta$, and natural $p$ have exact residue buckets and the required occurrence and cover data for $w$'s output.
--
--   Assume the terminal layout, source-value and sum word bounds, terminal space and word bounds, $S\le\Omega$, and depth
--   $$d+|\mathcal F_k|+\binom{2h(J-k)}{h(J-k)}+512hJ+11\le\Delta.$$
--   The routine returns a Boolean satisfying
--   $$r=1\iff \exists P\in\mathcal F_k,\ H(P),$$
--   where $\mathcal F_k$ is the frontier of $I,w$ and $H(P)$ is the guarded terminal test: an admissible enumerated completion has bucket-matching $u,v$ with $a_0+L_u=R_v$. It preserves memory before the terminal masks and uses the frontier-scan time bound plus $600$.
--
--   This connects stored frontier records to terminal checking.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightReportingTerminalStored.lean#L47-L149

